/T (Pregnancy is the period during which a fetus develops inside the uterus. The source guide describes a typical pregnancy as about 40 weeks, beginning from the first day of the last menstrual period. Common early signs can include a missed period, nausea or vomiting, fatigue, breast tenderness, and frequent urination. A home pregnancy test or healthcare visit can help confirm pregnancy.)
